{"parentUuid":"b276e481-0f9e-462d-8669-cc1ccf664db7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6b8557a2-9430-4f17-946a-1ea07dab5643","agentId":"ace34c9d71e0db288","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FpBBQ8RHUTMds5Xbm1sbbX","type":"tool_result","content":"f860ff3 codex: bash-tool-result cell supported, recorded in runs/shell-exit-status (#91)\nbd7e1e2 rules: a recording outranks a doc; partial support is supported with deviations; unsupported may be shown by runs (#90)\ncfd2711 rules: judge per unit (subjects), module.yaml is the agent's, module-distinct (#89)\nstatement: >-\n  Stop hooks that block keep the turn going only a limited number of times in\n  a row; once the limit is reached, the next block is overridden and the turn\n  ends. (A stop hook that only gives the agent context, without blocking, is\n  not part of this.)\nproviders:\n  claude:\n    docs:\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#stop-input\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#stop-decision-control\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#subagentstop-input\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks-guide#stop-hook-hits-the-block-cap\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/env-vars#variables\n    runs:\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/cap\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/cap-sub\n  codex: pending\n  cursor: pending\ncommit f860ff366b50328d62a3ff06a1cd76d39e84245f\nAuthor: Mykyta Svyrydenko <<redacted-email>>\nDate:   Sat Oct 3 16:44:15 2026 +0200\n\n    codex: bash-tool-result cell supported, recorded in runs/shell-exit-status (#91)\n    \n    Codex tells the agent a failed command's output like a success's; the failure is only in the event stream's command_execution item (status failed, exit_code). Recorded with the real codex; the cell lists that as a deviation, and the mock does the same.\n    \n    Co-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n codex-mock/e2e/001_hooks/shell_result_test.go      | 72 ++++++++++++++++++