{"parentUuid":"d8fe1b56-a66d-4d7c-a6f9-8f0b1f56c84e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6b8557a2-9430-4f17-946a-1ea07dab5643","agentId":"ace34c9d71e0db288","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Lys14WLJaAYuvXYnYEkaTn","type":"tool_result","content":"statement: >-\n  When a stop hook blocks, its reason is handed back to the agent, the turn\n  goes on, and the caller sees a single result at the turn's real end. (A stop\n  hook that only gives the agent context, without blocking, is not part of\n  this.)\nproviders:\n  claude:\n    docs:\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#stop-decision-control\n      - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks#exit-code-2-behavior-per-event\n    runs:\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/stops\n      - claude-mock/snapshots/runs/cap\n  codex:\n    docs:\n      - https://developers.openai.com/codex/hooks#stop\n    runs:\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/stops\n      - codex-mock/snapshots/runs/hook-exit-codes\n  cursor: pending\n{\"event\":\"hook\",\"hook\":\"SessionStart\",\"payload\":{\"session_id\":\"<SESSION_ID>\",\"hook_event_name\":\"SessionStart\",\"permission_mode\":\"bypassPermissions\",\"source\":\"startup\"}}\n{\"event\":\"hook\",\"hook\":\"UserPromptSubmit\",\"payload\":{\"session_id\":\"<SESSION_ID>\",\"hook_event_name\":\"UserPromptSubmit\",\"permission_mode\":\"bypassPermissions\",\"prompt\":\"Make every shell command its own separate tool call, never combined with another com\n{\"event\":\"hook\",\"hook\":\"PreToolUse\",\"payload\":{\"session_id\":\"<SESSION_ID>\",\"hook_event_name\":\"PreToolUse\",\"permission_mode\":\"bypassPermissions\",\"tool_name\":\"Bash\",\"tool_input\":{\"command\":\"echo DENYME\"}}}\n{\"event\":\"hook\",\"hook\":\"PreToolUse\",\"payload\":{\"session_id\":\"<SESSION_ID>\",\"hook_event_name\":\"PreToolUse\",\"permission_mode\":\"bypassPermissions\",\"tool_name\":\"Bash\",\"tool_input\":{\"command\":\"echo EXIT2ME\"}}}\n{\"event\":\"hook\",\"hook\":\"PreToolUse\",\"payload\":{\"session_id\":\"<SESSION_ID>\",\"hook_event_name\":\"PreToolUse\",\"permission_mode\":\"bypassPermissions\",\"tool_name\":\"Bash\",\"tool_input\":{\"command\":\"echo FINE\"}}}\n{\"event\":\"hook\",\"hook\":\"PostToolUse\",\"payload\":{\"session_id\":\"<SESSION_ID>\",\"hook_event_name\":\"PostToolUse\",\"permission_mode\":\"bypassPermissions\",\"tool_name\":\"Bash\",\"tool_input\":{\"command\":\"echo FINE\"},\"tool_response\":\"FINE\\n\"}}\n{\"event\":\"hook\",\"hook\":\"Stop\",\"payload\":{\"session_id\":\"<SESSION_ID>\",\"hook_event_name\":\"Stop\",\"permission_mode\":\"bypassPermissions\",\"stop_hook_active\":false}}\n{\"event\":\"hook\",\"hook\":\"Stop\",\"payload\":{\"session_id\":\"<SESSION_ID>\",\"hook_event_name\":\"Stop\",\"permission_mode\":\"bypassPermissions\",\"stop_hook_active\":true}}\n{\"event\":\"hook\",\"hook\":\"Stop\",\"payload\":{\"session_id\":\"<SESSION_ID>\",\"hook_event_name\":\"Stop\",\"permission_mode\":\"bypassPermissions\",\"stop_hook_active\":true}}\n{\"event\":\"stream\",\"type\":\"thread.started\",\"subtype\":null}\n{\"event\":\"stream\",\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"subtype\":\"error\"}\n{\"event\":\"stream\",\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"subtype\":\"error\"}\n{\"event\":\"stream\",\"type\":\"turn.started\",\"subtype\":null}\n{\"event\":\"stream\",\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"subtype\":\"agent_message\"}\n{\"event\":\"stream\",\"type\":\"item.started\",\"subtype\":\"command_execution\"}\n{\"event\":\"stream\",\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"subtype\":\"command_execution\"}\n{\"event\":\"stream\",\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"subtype\":\"agent_message\"}\n{\"event\":\"stream\",\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"subtype\":\"agent_message\"}\n{\"event\":\"stream\",\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"subtype\":\"agent_message\"}\n{\"event\":\"stream\",\"type\":\"turn.completed\",\"subtype\":null}\n(eval):1: no matches found: --include=*.go\n---\nconcern: \"what grounds a capability: the real harness for what it does, the user for what is mocked\"\nsloprails: [file-guard/capability-grounded, file-guard/capability-rigor]\n---\n\n# A capability states only what its harnesses document or were recorded doing\n\n## Concern\n\nA capability's statement is what every mock providing it claims about the real\nharness. It has two grounds: the real harness, for what it does (its docs and\nrecorded runs), and the user, for which of that is mocked and where a mock\nknowingly differs. A claim neither grounds is a mock inventing behaviour; a\nclaim only one harness makes, stated as everyone's, is a mock copying another's\nquirks.\n\n## Decision\n\n- A capability's `statement` (`spec/capabilities/<id>.yaml`) is\n  harness-neutral: what differs between providing harnesses (a default, a\n  name, a wire format) is left out of it.\n- For a supported cell, each part of the statement is either stated by the\n  harness's cited doc sections (`providers.<harness>.docs`, frozen by sha256 in\n  `<harness>-mock/snapshots/MANIFEST.yaml`), or shown by one of its cited runs\n  (`providers.<harness>.runs`: `<harness>-mock/snapshots/runs/<name>/`, whose\n  `samples/<ts>/` hold the real harness's payloads, stream and transcript), or\n  listed in the cell's `deviations` as a part the harness does not do.\n- A cell `{supported: false, reason, docs?, runs?}` claims the harness lacks\n  the behaviour, and is grounded by evidence of the same two kinds, at least\n  one: `runs`, recordings whose scenario attempts the behaviour and whose\n  samples show the real harness not doing it, and/or `docs` that show the\n  feature absent or cover the whole area without it; the judge reads them for\n  that. A harness whose recordings show only some parts of the statement is\n  supported, and the parts it does not do are its `deviations`. A `pending`\n  cell claims nothing and grounds nothing.\n- A recording outranks a doc: where a recorded run and a doc sentence\n  disagree, what the real harness was recorded doing is what it does. A cell\n  is supported when its recordings show the behaviour, whatever a doc says\n  elsewhere, and unsupported when its recordings show the behaviour not\n  happening, even where a doc describes it.\n- Adding or removing a capability, or changing its `statement`, carries the\n  user's words on its commit (`Sloprail-Cites-User`): the statement is the\n  capability the user wants implemented.\n- A cell's `deviations` need no user words: they are found empirically or\n  follow from other ADRs (e.g. a mock does not wait out a 5-minute background\n  limit, so e2e stays fast).","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"641f62ee-8fcf-4fe5-8d5b-d7408bde2713","timestamp":"2026-10-03T14:49:24.011Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d8fe1b56-a66d-4d7c-a6f9-8f0b1f56c84e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/nsviridenko/ws/sloprail/harness-mocks/.claude/worktrees/agent-ace34c9d71e0db288","sessionId":"f103aecd-8ff6-40a5-ad21-f5bd02338666","version":"2.1.286","gitBranch":"worktree-agent-a4d84e01b97891e91"}
